    "summary_one_sentence": "When an attempt to free a stuck anchor capsizes their boat during a storm in the Gulf of Mexico, four friends are left stranded on an overturned hull in a desperate struggle for survival.",
    "summary_short": "Based on a harrowing true story, four friends—including two NFL players—embark on an offshore fishing trip off the Florida coast. When their vessel capsizes in rough waters, leaving them without life vests or emergency gear, the men are trapped on the overturned boat facing severe hypothermia, dehydration, and massive waves. As time rapidly runs out, the U.S. Coast Guard battles treacherous weather conditions in a relentless search-and-rescue mission to locate them.",
    "summary_long": "Based on Nick Schuyler's best-selling memoir, 'Not Without Hope' tells the tragic true story of four athletic friends who set off on a day trip 70 miles out into the Gulf of Mexico. When their anchor becomes trapped on the seabed as a fierce storm approaches, an attempt to forcefully dislodge it causes the boat to capsize, throwing all four men into choppy, freezing waters. With no communication devices, fresh water, or life jackets, the friends cling to the slick, overturned hull as ten-to-twelve-foot waves continually batter them. Meanwhile, back on shore, anxious families alert the authorities, prompting U.S. Coast Guard Captain Timothy Close to organize an extensive air and sea search. As hours turn into days, the men endure extreme physical exhaustion, dehydration, and hypothermia-induced hallucinations. The friends push their physical and mental limits to keep each other anchored, physically and emotionally, against the relentless ocean. The narrative toggles between the agonizing struggle for survival at sea and the high-stakes rescue efforts mounted on land. Ultimately, the film stands as a powerful testament to brotherhood, resilience, and the endurance of human hope amidst overwhelming adversity.",
    "synopsis": "Based on extraordinary real-life events, 'Not Without Hope' follows trainer Nick Schuyler, his friend Will Bleakley, and NFL players Marquis Cooper and Corey Smith as they head out for a day of fishing in the Gulf of Mexico. When an unexpected accident capsizes their boat miles from land, the four companions find themselves stranded on the bottom of the vessel in the middle of an impending storm. Cut off from rescue and vulnerable to the unforgiving marine environment, they must rely on their physical conditioning and deep bond to stay alive. As the U.S. Coast Guard launches a massive search effort amidst deteriorating weather conditions, the story delivers an inspiring and tension-filled look at survival, love, and human endurance.",
